title: Hetzner worker server type falls back to cx32, the control-plane default is
  cpx21
updated: 2026-10-31T06:23:22Z
---

Found under k298 (2026-10-31). Since k298, a Hetzner control plane takes missing placement from `OCP::Config::%HETZNER_DEFAULTS` (cpx21 / fsn1 / debian-13). `OCP::Provider::Hetzner::create_server` (Provider/Hetzner.pm:129 and :274, POD :171/:191) still falls back to `cx32` at its last rank. So a Hetzner worker from `ocp node add` or robocop whose OCPNode and OCPNodeProvider name no server type gets cx32, while the control-plane default is cpx21.

Decision for the maintainer: should workers share the control-plane default (one source, cpx21 at today's value), keep cx32 as a separate worker default (then name it next to HETZNER_DEFAULTS and say why), or have no fallback (refuse a worker without a server type)? Switching changes what new workers cost, so it needs a Changes bullet. Related: k264 checks cpx21 against the live catalogue.
